# Numeric compensation answers, notice parsing and resume-review logging
Workstream-ID: lea-04
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/5
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: TODO.md, 2026-07-20 numeric-answer batch and supporting follow-ups
Status: DONE
Milestone: Configured numeric answers and visible resume decisions
Dependencies: None

## Purpose
Record the implemented numeric-answer and resume-log batch without publishing
any applicant's compensation, notice period or private configuration.

## Tasks
- [x] Prefer configured numeric notice days for day-specific questions.
- [x] Calculate monthly current compensation from configured annual compensation.
- [x] Implement the original monthly expected calculation and numeric rounding.
- [x] Emit plain numeric monetary answers without currency symbols or separators.
- [x] Log the resume choice before a configurable review pause; omit the pause in scan.
- [x] Correct local-calendar daily-count comparisons in database queries.
- [x] Add focused tests and update configuration/lifecycle documentation.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Numeric parsing, monthly calculations, tags and notice-day paths have recorded coverage.
- [x] The technical batch is distinguishable from later tier-policy overrides.

## Completion evidence
The legacy source records 12 salary/notice cases, a 121-test green suite and clean
Ruff/Black/mypy checks. It also records the local-date database correction.
Expected-compensation policy evolved later in lea-05 and lea-06; the original
rounding behavior is historical, not the current policy to restore.
DONE covers the recorded implementation/local-verification batch. Historical
review/live-test/publication follow-through is not represented as newly satisfied.
No actual compensation or notice values are included.

## Completion log
- 2026-07-20: Original numeric-answer and resume-log implementation recorded.
- 2026-07-21: Monthly rounding and local-date correction recorded in follow-up evidence.
- 2026-11-06: Created the bounded public-safe historical projection; no product behavior changed.
